[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   TEP-9 step 100 -- Cross-channel clock-consistency synthesis
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   The TEP-9 anomaly is fundamentally a claim about *clocks*: orbital
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   periods (macroscopic dynamical clocks) are the resident/transit
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   channels, while the spacecraft program adds three microscopic
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   channels -- the electronic quartz oscillator (SCLK), the plasma
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   frequency (PWS), and the nuclear decay clock (RTG).  Under TEP's
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   conformal coupling these process classes need not share one
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   effective coupling strength (screening factors and disformal terms
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   are process-dependent), so the correct question is not "do all
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   channels show the anomaly" but "are the measured/bounded values in
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   each channel mutually consistent with a single lapse field".
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   This step assembles the cross-channel ledger:
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   channel        clock class         observable              result
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   -------------  ------------------  ----------------------  ------------------
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   TNO resident   orbital dynamics     cap-clustered alignment  p = 0.0073 (44 obj)
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   comet transit  orbital dynamics     aphelion-dir slip        delta t/t ~ 1e-2
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   SCLK           electronic quartz    onboard-vs-ground rate   |dA/A| < ~2e-5
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   SCLK phase     electronic quartz    segment phase residuals  |dphi| < 0.16 s
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   PWS            plasma oscillation   f_pe structure           deltaX ~ 1.05
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   RTG            nuclear decay        power-decline slope      |dalpha| < ~1e-4
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   Reading the ledger
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   * The comet-channel slip is a *cumulative* integrated quantity
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   accrued along a transit through the boundary sector; the SCLK
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   bound is an *instantaneous* onboard-vs-ground rate ratio.  A
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   lapse field whose contrast is built across a transit region can
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   satisfy both simultaneously.
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   * The PWS lapse-equivalent shows the measured f_pe structure needs
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   a constants-shift ~1000x larger than the comet-channel lapse
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   contrast, confirming the structure is real plasma -- the channel
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   that a plasma-coupled screening transition would use as its
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   trigger.
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   * The RTG bound applies to the nuclear sector specifically; at
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   ~1e-4 in effective alpha it is consistent with a process-
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   dependent coupling where the nuclear clock's sensitivity differs
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   from the orbital channel's.
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   * Geometry: both Voyager paths thread the anti-axis hemisphere;
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   V1's asymptote and both craft's positions sit inside the mirror
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   cap, so the channels sample the second lobe of the bipolar slip
[2026-09-20 12:19:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 100]   field (step 089).
